{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3235-74c4-9518-5c7174543e28","id":"01a1a671-da09-7374-bab5-34c134781882","idempotency_key":"3f8abaf079da5d2397703b9a8e00debdb9c7e419aa5ca8208f37bd7d3dc2a31e","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T12:04:01Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-0314","note":"a test exports both ways and asserts neither study updated stamp nor version moved.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-c76d/i-0314"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3235-74c4-9518-5c7174543e28","id":"01a1a671-f3df-705a-a9c2-65c4aab51538","idempotency_key":"cf21b8a29fdf7c371c22278bcfdbf508333bace39d345447ae21d4a673ade67a","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T12:04:08Z","payload":{"note":"Closed 4/4. to_markdown writes the comparison as Markdown a person can paste into a review - study fields, per-chapter changes, boards, moves, shapes, annotations and notes - and GET /api/compare?format=markdown serves it; the Compare tab has an Export Markdown button that downloads diff.md. The report derives Serialize AND Deserialize, so an exported JSON round-trips: a test reads it back and asserts the re-serialisation is byte-identical. The Lua block is present and null, deliberately: a field that exists and is null today can be filled in R2 without changing the document's shape, which is what 'reserved' should mean. A test exports both ways and asserts neither study's updated stamp nor version counter moved. TWO PRODUCT BUGS the browser check found: every chapter was reported as changed because 'primary board' compared board IDs, which never match between two studies - it compares the primary board's TITLE now, so a chapter whose position did not move reports unchanged, and the chapter's own change flag now follows what is inside it rather than only its own fields; and the changed/all filter did nothing because the render closure read filter.get_untracked(), so the list never re-rendered on a filter change. Two more in the check itself: it picked rows by position, so it compared studies left over from earlier runs instead of the pair it had just seeded (it selects by title now).","target":"t-c76d"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
